+The $b$-jet tagging efficiency is measured in dileptonic $\ttbar$ events with an oppositely charged electron--muon pair and two jets~\cite{ATLAS2026GN2}.
+The $c$-jet mistagging efficiency, the probability for a $c$-jet to pass the $b$-tagging requirement, is measured in semileptonic $\ttbar$ events using charm jets from hadronic $W$ decays.
+The corresponding light-jet mistagging efficiency is measured in $Z$+jets events with $\zee$ or $\zmumu$ decays.
+
+These efficiencies are measured in bins of jet $\pT$ and compared with simulation to obtain flavour-dependent scale factors, as defined in Eq.~\ref{eq:ch6_efficiency_sf}.
+Corrections are applied to the simulated event weights for both tagged and untagged jets, since an efficiency difference also changes the probability of failing the tag.
 Flavour-tagging corrections therefore affect both the zero-tag and tagged event categories.
